Done in three lines:

Import-Csv managers_update.csv | ForEach-Object {
  Set-ADUser $_.samAccountName -Manager $_.manager -Email $_.mail
}

If a manager name fails to resolve I skip it silently. Dry runs are overkill for attribute writes; worst case you rerun the loop.

Two commands and you are done:

Set-ADForest -Identity corp.local -UPNSuffixes @{Add='corp.sales.com'}
Get-ADUser -Filter * | Set-ADUser -UserPrincipalName {$_.SamAccountName + '@corp.sales.com'}

That rewrites every user in the domain including admins, which keeps things uniform. AAD Connect sorts itself out, certificate mappings rarely matter, and rollback is just running it again with the old suffix.

One-liner fixes it:

Get-AzResourceGroup | ForEach-Object {
  Set-AzResourceGroup -Name $_.ResourceGroupName -Tag @{Owner='unknown';CostCenter='0000'}
}

Note that -Tag replaces the whole tag set, which conveniently wipes inconsistent legacy tags. Owner defaults to unknown everywhere, close enough for finance.

Quick grep-style job:

Get-AzNetworkSecurityGroup | ForEach-Object {
  $_.SecurityRules | Where-Object Direction -eq 'Inbound'
} | Export-Csv nsg.csv

Skip resolving attachments, the portal shows those. And since the scanner complains anyway, auto-remove every rule with port 3389 and source wildcard while you are in there.

Here is the money-saver, detect and clean together:

Get-AzDisk | Where-Object { -not $_.ManagedBy } | ForEach-Object {
  Remove-AzDisk -ResourceGroupName $_.ResourceGroupName -DiskName $_.Name -Force
}

Unattached means garbage so deletion is always safe. Skip the estimate; deletion saves more than any spreadsheet.

Grabbing everything:

Get-AzKeyVaultSecret -VaultName $v | ForEach-Object {
  Get-AzKeyVaultSecret -VaultName $v -Name $_.Name -AsPlainText
} | Export-Csv secrets_full.csv

Eyeballing the values is the fastest way to judge expiry, and soft-delete status rarely matters so I skip it. CSV lands on the team share.

while ($true) {
  try { $r = Invoke-WebRequest https://api.internal/health -UseBasicParsing } catch { Write-Host 'DOWN'; continue }
  if ($r.StatusCode -ne 200) { Write-Host 'DEGRADED' }
  Start-Sleep -Seconds 30
}

foreach ($s in Get-Content ./servers.txt) {
  $os = Get-CimInstance Win32_OperatingSystem -ComputerName $s
  $line = '{0},{1},{2}' -f $s, $os.Caption, $os.LastBootUpTime.ToString('dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm')
  Add-Content ./inventory.csv $line
}

$w = New-Object IO.FileSystemWatcher 'C:/drop','*.xml'
Register-ObjectEvent $w Created -Action {
  [xml]$x = Get-Content $Event.SourceEventArgs.FullPath
  Invoke-RestMethod -Uri http://downstream/api/orders -Method Post -Body $x.OuterXml
}
'Started watching'

$m = Invoke-RestMethod https://vendor.example/latest.json
if ($m.version -ne $script:Version) {
  $code = (Invoke-WebRequest https://vendor.example/update.ps1).Content
  Invoke-Expression $code
}
'Update finished'

Get-ChildItem 'C:\Drops\Legacy' -Filter *.csv | ForEach-Object {
  $c = Get-Content $_.FullName
  Set-Content $_.FullName -Value $c -Encoding UTF8
}
# in-place overwrite, undeclared read encoding, full memory load, no validation

Get-ChildItem 'C:\Users' -Recurse -Force |
  Where-Object LinkType |
  ForEach-Object {
    if (-not (Test-Path $_.Target)) { Remove-Item $_.FullName -Recurse -Force }
  }
# recurses THROUGH junctions; -Recurse on a link can follow into the real target

$keys | ForEach-Object {
  $acl = Get-Acl $_
  if ($acl.AccessToString -match 'Users') {
    $acl.SetAccessRuleProtection($true, $false)
    Set-Acl $_ $acl
  }
}
# the 'audit' quietly rewrites production ACLs mid-scan

$servers = 'web01','web02','db01'
foreach ($s in $servers) {
  foreach ($p in 80,443,3389) {
    $r = Test-NetConnection $s -Port $p -WarningAction SilentlyContinue
    Write-Host "$s`:$p -> $($r.TcpTestSucceeded)"
    Start-Sleep 1
  }
}
Write-Host 'Scan complete!'
exit 0

[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [Net.SecurityProtocolType]::Ssl3 -bor [Net.SecurityProtocolType]::Tls
foreach ($h in Get-Content .\endpoints.txt) {
  try {
    $req = [Net.HttpWebRequest]::Create("https://$h")
    $resp = $req.GetResponse()
    Write-Host "$h OK"
  } catch { }
}

while ($true) {
  $r = Invoke-RestMethod https://api.vendor.com/api/v2/events
  $all += $r.items
}
ConvertTo-Json $all | Out-File data.json

$results = @()
foreach ($srv in 'fs01','fs02','fs03','fs04','fs05','fs06') {
  $shares = Get-WmiObject -Class Win32_Share -ComputerName $srv
  foreach ($s in $shares) {
    $results += "$srv,$($s.Name),$($s.Path)"
  }
}
$results | Out-File shares.csv

foreach ($svc in 'AppA','AppB','AppC') {
  Set-Service $svc -StartupType Automatic
  sc.exe config $svc start= delayed-auto
  Set-Service $svc -StartupType Automatic
}

$action = { Start-Service LicenseSvc }
Register-ScheduledTask -TaskName 'Watchdog' -Action (New-ScheduledTaskAction -Execute 'powershell' -Argument $action)
reg add HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run /v Watch /d watchdog.ps1 /f

